    "title": "sarimasri3/Intersection-Conflict-Detection: Initial Release of Intersection Conflict Detection System",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14171746",
    "publication_date": "2024-11-15",
    "description": "<p>This is the initial release of the Intersection Conflict Detection and Management System.</p>\n<h3>Key Features:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Conflict Detection</strong>: Detects potential conflicts between vehicles at intersections using AI.</li>\n<li><strong>Priority Assignment</strong>: Applies traffic rules to assign priority levels to vehicles.</li>\n<li><strong>Waiting Time Calculation</strong>: Computes waiting times for vehicles to resolve conflicts.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Generation</strong>: Generates datasets with realistic intersection scenarios for training AI models.</li>\n<li><strong>GPT Fine-Tuning</strong>: Fine-tunes GPT models for traffic conflict classification.</li>\n<li><strong>LLAMA Fine-Tuning</strong>: Leverages LLAMA models for conflict detection with high accuracy.</li>\n<li><strong>Unit Testing</strong>: Includes comprehensive unit tests to ensure reliability.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Repository Structure:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>src/</strong>: Core functionality for conflict detection and data generation.</li>\n<li><strong>gpt_finetuning/</strong>: Scripts for fine-tuning GPT models.</li>\n<li><strong>llama_finetuning/</strong>: Scripts for fine-tuning LLAMA models.</li>\n<li><strong>tests/</strong>: Unit tests for the system.</li>\n<li><strong>data/</strong>: Contains datasets and intersection layout details.</li>\n<li><strong>images/</strong>: Illustrative figures and workflow diagrams.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Installation:</h3>\n<p>Refer to the <a href=\"https://github.com/sarimasri3/Intersection-Conflict-Detection#readme\">README.md</a> for detailed installation and usage instructions.</p>\n<h3>Related Research:</h3>\n<p>This release is part of the research described in the paper:\n<strong>&quot;Leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) for Traffic Management at Urban Intersections: The Case of Mixed Traffic Scenarios&quot;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Authors</strong>: Sari Masri, Huthaifa I. Ashqar, Mohammed Elhenawy</li>\n<li><strong>Preprint Link</strong>: <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.00948\">arXiv:2408.00948</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Licensing:</h3>\n<p>This project is licensed under the MIT License. See the <code>LICENSE</code> file for more details.</p>",
